    array.push(cH, "The Fed's own minutes said what the speakers have been saying all week: more hikes are coming.|A cooler UK inflation print yesterday, a hawkish set of Fed minutes last night: both nudges point the same way.|Hawkish minutes gave the dollar side another push, while Tokyo stayed with words rather than action.|The fear gauge slipped back under 25, so the franc's comeback trigger is no longer live, only close.|Oil slid again and the Fed minutes leaned hawkish: two winds blowing in the dollar's favour.|Australia lost 43,500 jobs in October, and the stand-off is now leaning clearly toward the dollar.|No news from Wellington again, while the Fed minutes kept the dollar's engine running.|France cleared one Senate hurdle, Britain is still digesting softer inflation, and the lean has not moved.|A Senate vote for the euro and a fresh warning for the yen, but neither moved this three-point lean.|With the VIX back under 25, the franc's route to a lean in this tie has closed for now.|The Aussie's jobs report collapsed overnight, and this euro-weak lean just lost some of its footing.|Only one side of this cross had news, and it did not help the euro.|Cheaper oil and a wider French spread: both legs got a little heavier, and the tie stays a tie.|The pound came out of its data run weaker, the yen held steady, and neither has a lead.|Both legs are on watch: a softer pound after CPI and a franc whose fear trigger just went quiet.|Australia's jobs shock lands in a pair that was already a stand-off.|Two currencies at +1 and a quiet night for both.|Oil sank again for the loonie, but the pound's own softness keeps this lean under watch.|The carry currency's labour market cracked overnight, and this three-point lean is now hanging by a thread.|High yield met a weak jobs report, while the haven's trigger cooled just below 25.|The Australian jobs report was the one release this cross was waiting for, and it went against the Aussie.|Both commodity currencies took a hit: jobs for the Aussie, oil for the loonie.|Wellington silent, Tokyo repeating itself: the stand-off continues.|The franc's fear trigger switched off at Wednesday's close, but only by a whisker.|Oil kept sliding, and that is the loonie's problem in this matchup.|Two legs held in place by rounding, and the night did not break either hold.|The franc's trigger cooled and the loonie's oil weighed: still no winner.|A haven duel where both havens have soft spots this morning.|Gold fell 3.5% after hawkish minutes, but its gap is set by inputs, and those did not change.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED (strengthened)~FOMC minutes: nearly all officials see more hikes as likely appropriate; Waller backs considering 50bp; December 25bp priced 90–95%.|CONFIRMED~Senate adopted the PLFSS 201–124 (deficit €14bn vs €12.7bn); OAT–Bund widened to 156.3bp on 17 Nov; CMP 26 Nov.|WEAKENED (watch)~No new BoE item; carried from CPI 3.6% below the BoE 3.7% projection (central +1, dovish R3 scenario still +1).|CONFIRMED (watch)~Katayama repeats US coordination and readiness to act (no action); BoJ December hike still expected; raw −0.9 held at 0.|WEAKENED (watch)~VIX closed 24.56 on 18 Nov, back below the 25 trigger met on 17 Nov; HY spread 3.43%; regime re-measured on Friday.|CONFIRMED (bearish reinforced)~Brent settled $91.95 (−1.3%), WTI $83.26 (−3.2%); no verified US–Canada deal; raw −4.5 held at −4.|INVALIDATED (bearish direction)~October jobs −43.5k vs +25k, unemployment 4.9% vs 4.7%: weakness condition met; shadow +3 central, 0 if R2 turns −1.|CONFIRMED~No NZ release or RBNZ remark after T0.|CONFIRMED (fragile)~Gold factor −3 unchanged; gold settled $3,728.80 (−3.5%), price context only; XAU shadow = G + USD shadow.")
    0
f_data21() =>
    array.push(cT, timestamp("Europe/Bucharest", 2026, 11, 19, 0, 0))
    array.push(cN, "Thu 19 Nov · evening")
    array.push(cD, "S-9,S-5,S6,P9,S10,X-3,S-5,W-4,F-3,T0,P-6,C-4,T1,T1,P4,T-2,T0,W5,P3,P6,T2,P7,T1,P4,S5,C-4,T-1,P-3,F-3")
    array.push(cH, "US factories wobbled today, yet the dollar's case barely flinched, and Paris had nothing to offer the euro.|Sterling sits at its lowest in a year against the greenback, and today's news did not hand it a rope.|Tokyo kept talking, the Fed kept leaning hawkish, and the pair stays tilted toward the dollar ahead of Japan's CPI.|Wall Street lurched lower and the fear gauge shot above 28 intraday: the franc's comeback trigger is back on.|Carney met Trump in Shenzhen and came back with warm words but no deal, while crude kept leaking lower.|A day after the jobs shock, rate markets dropped every trace of another RBA hike.|The kiwi found some support from its own rate market, but not enough to change the matchup.|Neither side moved on the scoreboard today; the pound's softer tone is still the open question.|Global stocks slid and the yen stayed steady, so this three-point lean keeps hanging by its thread.|The fear trigger that favours the franc lit up again, but this tie needs a score change to break.|The Aussie's rate story turned from 'one more hike?' to 'when is the first cut?', and that eats into this lean.|New Zealand's rate market still expects a hike, which keeps the kiwi a step ahead of a stuck euro.|Canada left Shenzhen empty-handed on the US deal, and the euro waited for Paris: still a coin toss.|The pound drifted and the yen waited for tonight's inflation figure: no lean yet.|Both legs went the wrong way for this lean today: a cautious Bailey and a frightened stock market.|Rate cuts are now priced for Australia, but even that does not create a winner here.|One central bank is still expected to hike, the other just trimmed its 2027 path: the scores stay level.|The loonie missed its US deal again, yet the softer pound keeps this lean under watch.|Risk-off and a dovish RBA repricing on the same day: the carry cross is losing both its supports.|A rate-cut story for the Aussie and a fear spike for the franc: this lean is being squeezed from both ends.|The two rate markets pulled apart today, cuts for Australia and a hike for New Zealand, but the scores have not.|Australia's rate market turned dovish just as Canada's US deal slipped again; the stronger leg is the one cracking.|The kiwi's hike odds and the yen's verbal shield both held: still no lean.|A risk scare is the franc's friend and the kiwi's enemy, and Thursday delivered one intraday.|Canada got no US deal and cheaper oil, while the kiwi kept its hike odds: the lean holds.|Two currencies held by rounding, one with a missed trade deal and one with an inflation test tonight.|The franc's fear trigger fired intraday and the loonie stayed heavy, but the tie survives on paper.|In this haven duel, the franc just got the risk shock its comeback condition describes.|Gold slipped again even as stocks fell, so the haven channel has not helped it yet.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED (strengthened)~Second-tier data mixed (claims 203k, Philly 6.3) but prices paid jumped to 58.2; hike path intact.|CONFIRMED~No new spread print after 156.3bp (17 Nov); Senate budget debate from Friday.|WEAKENED (watch)~Bailey balanced (no pre-set path); 2027 BoE pricing trimmed to 80bp.|CONFIRMED (watch)~Katayama repeats the warning; December BoJ hike expected; CPI tonight.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~VIX 27–28 intraday meets the franc condition (two consistent sources); close pending; score re-measured Friday.|CONFIRMED (bearish reinforced)~Carney after meeting Trump: deal possible but not yet there; oil lower.|INVALIDATED (bearish direction)~Swaps price no RBA hike and a 68% cut by June; shadow +3 central, 0 if R2 is cut.|CONFIRMED~RBNZ 25bp hike priced at 78%; no score change.|CONFIRMED (fragile)~Gold factor −3 unchanged; XAU shadow +3 only via the USD shadow.")
    0
f_data22() =>
    array.push(cT, timestamp("Europe/Bucharest", 2026, 11, 20, 0, 0))
    array.push(cN, "Fri 20 Nov · morning")
    array.push(cD, "S-9,S-5,S8,P9,S10,X-3,S-5,W-4,X-1,T0,P-6,C-4,T1,X3,P4,T-2,T0,W5,P5,P6,T2,P7,X3,P4,C5,X-2,T-1,X-1,F-3")
    array.push(cH, "Wall Street had its worst day in weeks, and the dollar still walked away with the stronger hand.|Sterling slept through the night while American shares tumbled, and the greenback kept its edge.|Tokyo's inflation came in a touch cooler than hoped, and the yen lost another piece of its story.|The fear gauge closed well above 25, and that is the franc's alarm bell ringing for real this time.|No news from Ottawa overnight, and the loonie's case stayed as soft as it was on Thursday.|The Aussie's bad week found no relief overnight, so the bearish shadow from Thursday holds.|The kiwi had no headlines of its own, which left the dollar to set the tone again.|Neither side spoke overnight, so this pair waits on London's shoppers and Lagarde's microphone.|Japan's softer core inflation took the bite out of the yen, and the bearish lean here slipped into a stand-off.|A genuine risk-off close lands right on this pair's fault line, but the scores have not moved yet.|The Aussie is still limping after Thursday's jobs shock, which keeps this bearish view under strain.|Two quiet currencies met overnight, and the bearish read stayed exactly where it was.|Still a stand-off: the euro's French trouble and the loonie's soft inflation cancel each other out.|A softer Japanese inflation print turned this stand-off into a pound lean, at least in the shadow.|The franc's fear trigger has now been met on a close, and that leans hard against this pound lean.|A stand-off between two leaking boats: the pound's soft inflation and the Aussie's jobs shock.|Level pegging again, with neither side giving the other an opening overnight.|The pound's softer week keeps this bullish view under watch, even with the loonie still weak.|Japan's cooler core CPI helped this pair on paper, but the Aussie's wound keeps it under pressure.|Weak Australian jobs on one side and a risk-off close on the other: this lean is under fire twice.|Still a draw, and the Aussie's weak jobs make a kiwi lean more likely than an Aussie one.|The Aussie's jobs hit keeps pressure on this bullish view, even though the loonie offered no help overnight.|The yen slipped on softer inflation, and this quiet stand-off tipped into a kiwi lean in the shadow.|A true risk-off close puts this kiwi lean on shaky ground ahead of Friday's measurement.|Two quiet commodity currencies, and the kiwi still holds the better hand.|The yen's soft inflation cut away the support under this bearish view, and the shadow now shows a stand-off.|Still a stand-off on the scores, but a risk-off regime tonight could break it toward the franc.|Japan's softer core inflation pulled the yen down, and this bearish lean drifted into a stand-off.|Gold kept sliding through a stock-market rout, so the haven story has not saved it yet.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED (strengthened)~Stocks fell 2% but December hike odds held near 96%; Barr: inflation too high.|CONFIRMED~No spread print after 156.3bp (17 Nov); Senate budget (PLF) debate opens today.|WEAKENED (watch)~No BoE item overnight; UK retail sales at 09:00 are the next test.|WEAKENED (watch)~Core CPI 2.2% vs 2.3% expected (second soft surprise after GDP): shadow −2; 0 if read as in line.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~VIX closed about 28.4: the franc condition is met on a close; score re-measured from Friday closes.|CONFIRMED (bearish reinforced)~No Canadian item overnight; retail sales at 15:30 Bucharest.|INVALIDATED (bearish direction)~Jobs-miss condition still met; shadow +3 central, 0 if the RBA outlook (R2) is cut.|CONFIRMED~No New Zealand item overnight; most exposed to a −2 risk regime at Friday close.|CONFIRMED (fragile)~Gold factor −3 unchanged (spot near $3,675); XAU shadow +3 only via the USD shadow.")
    0
if barstate.isfirst
    f_data0()
    f_data1()
    f_data2()
    f_data3()
    f_data4()
    f_data5()
    f_data6()
    f_data7()
    f_data8()
    f_data9()
    f_data10()
    f_data11()
    f_data12()
    f_data13()
    f_data14()
    f_data15()
    f_data16()
    f_data17()
    f_data18()
    f_data19()
    f_data20()
    f_data21()
    f_data22()

// ───────── helpers ─────────
f_item(string row, int i) =>
    string[] parts = str.split(row, ",")
    i >= 0 and i < array.size(parts) ? array.get(parts, i) : "?"
f_bname(string b) => b == "U" ? "BULLISH" : b == "D" ? "BEARISH" : b == "N" ? "TWO-SIDED" : "none"
f_cname(string c) => c == "h" ? "high" : c == "m" ? "medium" : c == "l" ? "low" : "-"
f_sg(float v) => na(v) ? "0" : v > 0 ? "+" + str.tostring(v) : str.tostring(v)
f_sname(string s) => s == "C" ? "Confirmed" : s == "S" ? "Confirmed, could get stronger" : s == "F" ? "Confirmed but fragile" : s == "W" ? "Under watch" : s == "P" ? "Under pressure" : s == "X" ? "Invalidated" : s == "T" ? "Still two-sided" : "none"
f_wa(bool ok) => ok ? "with" : "against"
var string[] DOW = array.from("Sun", "Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat")

// ───────── pair and week ─────────
string symA = syminfo.basecurrency + syminfo.currency
string tk   = str.upper(syminfo.ticker)
string symB = str.length(tk) >= 6 ? str.substring(tk, 0, 6) : tk
int pIdx = pairIn != "Auto" ? array.indexof(PAIRS, pairIn) : array.indexof(PAIRS, symA) >= 0 ? array.indexof(PAIRS, symA) : array.indexof(PAIRS, symB)
string pName = pIdx >= 0 ? array.get(PAIRS, pIdx) : syminfo.ticker
float pipSz = str.contains(pName, "JPY") ? 0.01 : str.contains(pName, "XAU") ? 0.1 : 0.0001
f_pips(float d) => math.round(d / pipSz * 10) / 10

int WEEK_MS = 7 * 86400000
var int wi = -1
while wi + 1 < array.size(wT) and time >= array.get(wT, wi + 1)
    wi += 1
bool inWk = wi >= 0 and time < array.get(wT, math.max(wi, 0)) + WEEK_MS
string rec = inWk and pIdx >= 0 ? f_item(array.get(wD, math.max(wi, 0)), pIdx) : "?"
bool hasRec = rec != "?" and str.length(rec) >= 2
string b  = hasRec ? str.substring(rec, 0, 1) : "-"
string cv = hasRec ? str.substring(rec, 1, 2) : "-"
float  g  = hasRec and str.length(rec) > 2 ? str.tonumber(str.substring(rec, 2)) : na

// latest daily check for this pair up to this bar
var int ci = -1
while ci + 1 < array.size(cT) and time >= array.get(cT, ci + 1)
    ci += 1
string ck = ci >= 0 and pIdx >= 0 ? f_item(array.get(cD, math.max(ci, 0)), pIdx) : "?"
string ckS = ck == "?" or ci < 0 or time - array.get(cT, math.max(ci, 0)) > 3 * 86400000 ? "none" : f_sname(str.substring(ck, 0, 1))

// ───────── direction ─────────
[dC1, dSma] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [close[1], ta.sma(close, 20)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
int biasDir = b == "U" ? 1 : b == "D" ? -1 : 0
bool convOk = minConv == "Any" or (minConv == "High only" ? cv == "h" : cv == "h" or cv == "m")
int bDir = convOk ? biasDir : 0
int tDir = na(dSma) ? 0 : dC1 > dSma ? 1 : dC1 < dSma ? -1 : 0
int dir = dirMode == "Fundamental bias" ? bDir : (bDir == tDir ? bDir : 0)
float atr = ta.atr(14)
int NY7 = 7 * 3600000
int tDay = dayofweek(time + NY7, "America/New_York")
int fri17 = timestamp("America/New_York", year(time + NY7, "America/New_York"), month(time + NY7, "America/New_York"), dayofmonth(time + NY7, "America/New_York"), 17, 0)
bool lastWkBar = tDay == dayofweek.friday and time_close + timeframe.in_seconds() * 1000 > fri17
int hB = hour(time, "Europe/Bucharest")
bool allow = (not hrsOn or (hB >= hrsFrom and hB < hrsTo)) and not (noFri and tDay == dayofweek.friday) and tDay != dayofweek.saturday and tDay != dayofweek.sunday and not lastWkBar

// ───────── structure (pivots confirmed after their right-hand candles close) ─────────
float pSH = ta.pivothigh(high, swLen, swLen)
float pSL = ta.pivotlow(low, swLen, swLen)
float pIH = ta.pivothigh(high, inLen, inLen)
float pIL = ta.pivotlow(low, inLen, inLen)
var float swH = na
var float swL = na
var float inH = na
var float inL = na
var int   inHi = na
var int   inLi = na
if not na(pSH)
    swH := pSH
if not na(pSL)
    swL := pSL
if not na(pIH)
    inH := pIH
    inHi := bar_index - inLen
if not na(pIL)
    inL := pIL
    inLi := bar_index - inLen

// ───────── setup: BOS → pullback into discount → internal CHoCH ─────────
var bool  sOn = false
var int   sD = 0
var float sLvl = na
var float sA = na
var float sExt = na
var int   sI = na
var float sPb = na
var int   sPbi = na
var float slLvl = na
var float tpLvl = na
var int   posDir = 0
var int   lastExitT = 0
var float ent0 = na
var box   zSl = na
var box   zTp = na
var int   zEb = -1
bool flat = strategy.position_size == 0
if not flat and posDir == 0
    posDir := strategy.position_size > 0 ? 1 : -1
if flat and posDir != 0
    if not na(zSl)
        box.set_right(zSl, bar_index)
    if not na(zTp)
        box.set_right(zTp, bar_index)
    posDir := 0
    lastExitT := time

bool bosNow = false
bool chochNow = false
bool active = flat and time >= fromT and dir != 0 and time - lastExitT >= coolH * 3600000 and not na(atr)
if active
    if sOn and sD != dir
        sOn := false
    float sh = dir > 0 ? swH : swL
    float lo = dir > 0 ? swL : swH
    if not na(sh) and (close - sh) * dir > 0 and (not sOn or sLvl != sh) and not na(lo)
        sOn := true
        sD := dir
        sLvl := sh
        sA := lo
        sExt := dir > 0 ? high : low
        sI := bar_index
        sPb := na
        sPbi := na
        bosNow := true
    else if sOn
        if bar_index - sI > maxWait or (close - sA) * dir < 0
            sOn := false
        else
            float lvl = sA + (1 - discPct / 100) * (sExt - sA)
            if na(sPb)
                sExt := dir > 0 ? math.max(sExt, high) : math.min(sExt, low)
                lvl := sA + (1 - discPct / 100) * (sExt - sA)
                if dir > 0 ? low <= lvl : high >= lvl
                    sPb := dir > 0 ? low : high
                    sPbi := bar_index
            else
                sPb := dir > 0 ? math.min(sPb, low) : math.max(sPb, high)
                float ih = dir > 0 ? inH : inL
                int ihI = dir > 0 ? inHi : inLi
                if not na(ih) and ihI > sPbi - 6 and (close - ih) * dir > 0 and allow
                    float sl = sPb - dir * slBuf * atr
                    float risk = math.abs(close - sl)
                    if risk > 0 and risk <= maxRisk * atr
                        float lq = dir > 0 ? swH : swL
                        float tp = tpMode == "None" ? na : tpMode == "Swing liquidity (min 2R)" and not na(lq) and (lq - close) * dir >= 2 * risk ? lq : close + dir * tpR * risk
                        float qRaw = strategy.equity * stRisk / 100 / (risk * syminfo.pointvalue)
                        float q = qRaw >= 20 ? math.floor(qRaw) : math.round(qRaw, 2)
                        string id = dir > 0 ? "L" : "S"
                        string cmt = pName + " | " + (dir > 0 ? "long" : "short") + " | bias " + f_bname(b) + " " + f_cname(cv) + " gap " + f_sg(g) + " | BOS " + str.tostring(sLvl, format.mintick) + " | CHoCH | SL " + str.tostring(f_pips(risk)) + "p | " + array.get(DOW, tDay - 1) + " " + timeframe.period
                        slLvl := sl
                        tpLvl := tp
                        ent0 := close
                        strategy.entry(id, dir > 0 ? strategy.long : strategy.short, qty = q, comment = cmt)
                        strategy.exit("X" + id, id, stop = sl, limit = tp, comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP")
                        chochNow := true
                    sOn := false

// ───────── exits ─────────
int prevBias = biasDir[1]
if not flat
    string id = posDir > 0 ? "L" : "S"
    strategy.exit("X" + id, id, stop = slLvl, limit = tpLvl, comment_loss = "SL", comment_profit = "TP")
    if wkExit and lastWkBar
        strategy.close(id, comment = "Friday close")
    else if flipEx and biasDir == -posDir and prevBias != biasDir
        strategy.close(id, comment = "Bias flip")

// ───────── drawing ─────────
if strOn and bosNow
    label.new(bar_index, dir > 0 ? high : low, "BOS", style = dir > 0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color = color.new(dir > 0 ? bullC : bearC, 30), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
if strOn and chochNow
    label.new(bar_index, dir > 0 ? low : high, "CHoCH", style = dir > 0 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = dir > 0 ? bullC : bearC, textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plot(strOn and sOn ? sLvl : na, "BOS level", color = color.new(color.gray, 30), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(strOn and sOn ? sA + (1 - discPct / 100) * (sExt - sA) : na, "Discount level", color = color.new(color.orange, 20), style = plot.style_linebr)
if not flat and zonesOn
    int eb = strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(0)
    float ep = strategy.opentrades.entry_price(0)
    if eb != zEb
        zEb := eb
        zSl := box.new(eb, math.max(ep, slLvl), bar_index, math.min(ep, slLvl), border_color = color.new(bearC, 30), bgcolor = color.new(bearC, 80))
        zTp := na(tpLvl) ? na : box.new(eb, math.max(ep, tpLvl), bar_index, math.min(ep, tpLvl), border_color = color.new(bullC, 30), bgcolor = color.new(bullC, 80))
    box.set_right(zSl, bar_index)
    if not na(zTp)
        box.set_right(zTp, bar_index)
bgcolor(dir > 0 ? color.new(bullC, 95) : dir < 0 ? color.new(bearC, 95) : na, title = "Direction")

var table tb = table.new(position.bottom_right, 2, 3, bgcolor = color.new(#1E222D, 10), border_width = 1)
if barstate.islast
    table.cell(tb, 0, 0, "BE Structure · " + pName, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 0, timeframe.period, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 1, "Bias", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 1, f_bname(b) + " " + f_cname(cv) + " " + f_sg(g), text_color = biasDir > 0 ? bullC : biasDir < 0 ? bearC : color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 2, "Setup", text_color = color.gray, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(tb, 1, 2, not flat ? "in trade" : sOn ? (na(sPb) ? "BOS, waiting for discount" : "in discount, waiting for CHoCH") : "waiting for BOS", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
if timeframe.period != "60" and barstate.islast
    label.new(bar_index, high, "BE Structure was tested on the 1H chart (pivot lengths are in chart candles).", style = label.style_label_down, color = color.orange, textcolor = color.white)
